{"v":2,"s":"p","w":2,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Every measurement has an error","b":"<p>No measurement is perfect. The smallest step on a scale is the <b>scale division</b> (podeok); the reading error is usually half of it.</p><p>The result is written as <b>x = x̄ ± Δx</b>, where x̄ is the mean value and Δx the <b>absolute error</b> (apsolutna greška).</p><div class=\"callout\">Measuring a table with a ruler: the error tells you how much to trust the last digit.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 86\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Reading a ruler with millimetre divisions: the edge is at 3.4 cm, give or take half a millimetre.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"280\" height=\"34\" rx=\"2\" class=\"sf\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"30\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">0</text><line x1=\"35.2\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"35.2\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"40.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"40.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"45.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"45.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"50.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"50.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"56\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"56\" y2=\"53\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"61.2\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"61.2\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"66.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"66.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"71.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"71.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"76.80000000000001\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"76.80000000000001\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"82\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"82\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">1</text><line x1=\"87.2\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"87.2\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"92.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"92.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"97.60000000000001\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"97.60000000000001\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"102.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"102.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"53\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"113.2\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"113.2\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"118.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"118.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"123.60000000000001\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"123.60000000000001\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"128.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"128.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"134\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"134\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"134\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">2</text><line x1=\"139.2\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"139.2\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"144.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"144.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"149.60000000000002\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"149.60000000000002\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"154.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"154.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"53\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"165.20000000000002\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"165.20000000000002\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"170.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"170.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"175.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"175.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"180.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"180.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"186\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"186\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"186\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">3</text><line x1=\"191.20000000000002\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"191.20000000000002\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"196.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"196.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"201.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"201.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"206.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"206.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"212\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"53\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"217.20000000000002\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"217.20000000000002\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"222.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"222.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"227.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"227.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"232.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"232.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"238\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"238\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"238\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">4</text><line x1=\"243.20000000000002\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"243.20000000000002\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"248.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"248.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"253.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"253.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"258.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"258.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"264\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"264\" y2=\"53\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"269.20000000000005\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"269.20000000000005\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"274.4\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"274.4\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"279.6\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"279.6\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"284.8\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"284.8\" y2=\"48\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"58\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"290\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"10\">5</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"14\" width=\"177\" height=\"22\" rx=\"2\" class=\"a2\"/><line x1=\"206.8\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"206.8\" y2=\"40\" class=\"kc\" /><text x=\"214\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">3.4 cm</text></svg><figcaption>Reading a ruler with millimetre divisions: the edge is at 3.4 cm, give or take half a millimetre.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Mean value and errors","b":"<p>Measure several times and take the mean: x̄ = (x₁ + x₂ + … + xₙ)/n. In school problems, the absolute error is often the largest deviation from the mean.</p><div class=\"fx\">relative error δ = Δx / x̄ · 100%</div><p>More measurements reduce random errors; they don’t fix a badly calibrated instrument (a systematic error).</p>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A pendulum period was measured as 12.1 s, 12.3 s and 12.2 s. Write the result.","s":["Mean: (12.1 + 12.3 + 12.2)/3 = 12.2 s.","Largest deviation: 0.1 s.","Relative error: 0.1/12.2 ≈ 0.8%."],"a":"T = (12.2 ± 0.1) s, about 0.8%"},{"t":"num","q":"Mean of 4.0, 4.2 and 4.4?","a":4.2,"u":"","e":"12.6 / 3.","tol":0.001},{"t":"num","q":"Relative error of (50 ± 1) cm, in %?","a":2,"u":"%","e":"1/50 · 100%."},{"t":"mc","q":"A ruler with mm divisions has a reading error of about:","o":["±1 cm","±0.5 mm","±5 mm","±0.1 mm"],"a":1,"e":"Half the smallest division."},{"t":"mc","q":"0.0042 in scientific notation:","o":["4.2·10⁻²","4.2·10⁻³","42·10⁻⁴","0.42·10⁻²"],"a":1,"e":"Move the decimal point 3 places."},{"t":"tf","q":"Repeating a measurement more times reduces random error.","a":true,"e":"Random errors average out; systematic errors don’t."}]}